Spec: Flip and Mirror

Purpose:
  Flip selected shapes horizontally or vertically around their collective center.

Owns:
  ./flip.ts
  ./flip.test.ts

Must:
  Flip horizontal mirrors shapes across the vertical axis of their bounding box center.
  Flip vertical mirrors shapes across the horizontal axis of their bounding box center.
  Work on single shapes and multi-selections.
  Work on all shape types (path, text, group).
  Preserve shape prototypes after flip (use clone pattern).
  Be fully undoable (FlipCommand implements Command interface).

Must not:
  Modify unselected shapes.
  Change the collective bounding box center position.
  Flip around the material center (flip around selection center).

Depends on:
  @IShape
  @useStore
  @Geometry.getCombinedBounds

Exposes:
  FlipCommand(shapes, axis)

Accepts:
  shapes: IShape[] (selected shapes)
  axis: 'horizontal' | 'vertical'

Scenario: flip horizontal
  Given a triangle at x=50, y=50 with width 100
  When the user flips horizontally
  Then the triangle's nodes are mirrored across x=100 (center of bounds)
  And the bounding box center remains at the same position

Scenario: flip vertical on group
  Given a group containing 3 shapes
  When the user flips vertically
  Then all children are mirrored across the group's vertical center
  And the group bounds remain in the same position

Scenario: undo flip
  Given a shape was flipped horizontally
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the shape returns to its original orientation

Tasks:
  [ ] Create FlipCommand class implementing Command interface.
  [ ] Implement horizontal flip (negate X relative to center).
  [ ] Implement vertical flip (negate Y relative to center).
  [ ] Handle PathShape nodes (mirror anchor + control points).
  [ ] Handle GroupShape (mirror all children recursively).
  [ ] Handle TextObject (mirror position and set scaleX/scaleY).
  [ ] Add unit tests for all shape types.
  [ ] Add keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+Shift+H / Ctrl+Shift+V or toolbar buttons).
  [ ] Add UI buttons in Properties panel.

Done when:
  FlipCommand passes unit tests for path, text, and group shapes.
  Undo restores original geometry exactly.
  UI buttons appear in the Properties panel operations section.
  Keyboard shortcuts are registered and documented.
